#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179522 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179667 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "db8e7d68-5731-5a44-b86e-919a13689540" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/id #uuid "b1f5f31f-55d0-5523-8225-03db04d35cb1" :question/math-academy-id "e-6248" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,2]\\times [1,3]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = x+2y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = x+2y$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/67/67daa328cc6ae4cb37be386c327fb4548844fad2adc10476bdf1147c5a5d4218.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top right corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/6e/6e58954fccd74eaf67c95df818c4c9050c35b324c5fffe4902a366cb295b8845.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j})={x}_{i}+2{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}+2{y}_{j})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179523 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179668 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5c07033-ef84-52e6-bd08-b1f0cc289e9f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/id #uuid "7215d75e-c001-5c28-a5e7-08a74f6543d7" :question/math-academy-id "e-6250" :question/problem "Let $R = [0,1] \\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f, P).$" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[0,1],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 90-x^2-y^2$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[0,2].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/5b/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=90-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(90-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179589 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing"}] :question/id #uuid "79b4e8e3-5cfd-5b28-ba19-f69d2c9e0c71" :question/math-academy-id "e-9495" :question/problem "Let $R = [2,4] \\times [0,1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y) = 2x - y.$ Further, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWrite down the upper Riemann sum $U(f,P).$" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $M_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion $R_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion $R_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between $x_{i-1}$ and $x_i$ over the $x$-axis and $y_{i-1}$ and $y_i$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that\n\n- $f(x,y) = 2x - y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y) = 2x - y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/de/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\leq i\\leq m$ and $1\\leq j\\leq n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(2{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256729 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d2e986b-5318-51ca-9180-ee9392d7b329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253783} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea23653-3024-5963-99a7-7200e3c51651" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{x}_{i}-{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254349} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac822a0-70fb-5ba4-b167-87fa282f53f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5{x}_{i-1}-{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254471} {:answer/id #uuid "8c187270-7988-5818-99a7-3f8432b8ae3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i-1}-11{y}_{j}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254908} {:answer/id #uuid "f47934f0-a0c4-5fe5-a38c-d9de05e491e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f47934f0-a0c4-5fe5-a38c-d9de05e491e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255813} :answer-field/id #uuid "a03842f3-818b-56ea-bd27-4547b0faf8bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256209}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4dff037f-4d65-5443-84ba-e0a047388826" :question/math-academy-id "q-122841" :question/problem "Let $R=[-2,2]\\times [-5,-1]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=7x-11y+5.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$\nwhat is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=7x-11y+5$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=7x-11y+5$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/de/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})=7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $7{x}_{i}-11{y}_{j-1}+5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544822 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "170bd9f4-1de2-54a2-9348-e26f2a20b717" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{y}_{j-1}-2{x}_{i-1}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544133} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec7b257-6e52-550f-bdbe-6ce6252546d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544398} {:answer/id #uuid "9efd5c77-2cb1-5be1-800e-6b69df9db58e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{y}_{j-1}-{x}_{i-1}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544431} {:answer/id #uuid "a320cf0c-d21a-5986-b52e-7e793989a2a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{y}_{j}+3{x}_{i}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544438} {:answer/id #uuid "ebaa5111-af23-5adf-b4a4-fb1b96aafaa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebaa5111-af23-5adf-b4a4-fb1b96aafaa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544596} :answer-field/id #uuid "edd2fc28-bb7b-522b-8b22-9cd25ae03847" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5cf5fafd-606c-53b3-9dcd-de496f0b8804" :question/math-academy-id "q-170684" :question/problem "Let $R=[-1,3]\\times [-4,-2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=8y-2x-5.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=8y-2x-5$ decreases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=8y-2x-5$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/ff/ffa57d3e7fed08212f12d4b9d7c2e0a4d33a3aac71c8b8a03d1a9a7364484deb.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *largest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *top left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/74/74d546d91e145efea49b70af56cb472e8bbbd1417725cd7fa92a3a278cad75ea.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j})=8{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(8{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}-5)Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $8{y}_{j}-2{x}_{i-1}-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b815d42d-8e8a-5036-b6c4-76e4c20b20b7" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Function That’s Neither Strictly Increasing nor Decreasing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ca49bbf-10a2-579d-8594-e9c65b020900" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}+5{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342479} {:answer/id #uuid "28febdac-2bba-5b11-bae9-95308bb0cf6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342582} {:answer/id #uuid "7713f00b-5ce0-5d6b-9b37-c5ee1d36f372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i-1}-3{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343270} {:answer/id #uuid "89cbe354-82b0-5598-a001-1f0b6e86a821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343436} {:answer/id #uuid "d6286248-1533-522f-bf0b-415f8d2586cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}+5{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89cbe354-82b0-5598-a001-1f0b6e86a821" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343436} :answer-field/id #uuid "c986c60e-cb0d-5493-902e-52c311d10e52" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344845}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8a3bcd08-2d96-5714-8501-bedb2f0a1010" :question/math-academy-id "q-75056" :question/problem "Let $R=[15,20]\\times [3,5]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=x-3y.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$\nwhat is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=x-3y$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x-3y$ decreases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](images/01/01b291ca7cd81b88cf6ed06fdcdb2ffcbb1f78255d0f57d496823d347c2fb0b3.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *largest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom right corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](images/de/de36b521dea1f925754a9c630c3d4a2c405c087a191138f1eaaa5771becb8c21.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i},{y}_{j-1})={x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}({x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is ${x}_{i}-3{y}_{j-1}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186180276 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179668 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a5c07033-ef84-52e6-bd08-b1f0cc289e9f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Decreasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae1aafb8-742c-5ecc-bd64-e83dcc16f18d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364380} {:answer/id #uuid "15dd553a-683c-59bf-86b8-c6b3df640237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364381} {:answer/id #uuid "7e233043-c00a-5ca5-82b9-beb10aa42e8e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30-{x}_{i}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364382} {:answer/id #uuid "09f61d58-b48b-5f8c-a045-0cad83ee2110" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{i-1}^{2}-2{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364383} {:answer/id #uuid "85f6283b-5714-5a77-9512-cc5f90a181d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85f6283b-5714-5a77-9512-cc5f90a181d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364384} :answer-field/id #uuid "ceb9984c-fe58-5443-8e27-fbc24911ec49" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186364379}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "acf35dbc-ce10-50e5-a111-5d65e31ca4ef" :question/math-academy-id "q-75097" :question/problem "Let $R=[2,5]\\times [0,2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x,y)=30-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.$\nFurther, let $P$ be a partition of $R,$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{1}=\\{{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}\\},\\,{P}_{2}=\\{{y}_{0},{y}_{1},…,{y}_{n}\\},\\,P={P}_{1}\\times {P}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the upper Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to $P$ is given by\n\n$$\nU(f,P)={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}\\boxed{}\\,Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\n$$\n\nwhere $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1}$ and $Δ{y}_{j}={y}_{j}-{y}_{j-1},$ what is the missing expression in the double summation above?" :question/worked-solution "The upper Riemann sum is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}{M}_{ij}Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${M}_{ij}$ is the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ \n\nWe consider an arbitrary subregion ${R}_{ij}$ of the partition. This subregion lies between ${x}_{i-1}$ and ${x}_{i}$ over the $x$-axis and ${y}_{i-1}$ and ${y}_{i}$ over the $y$-axis, as shown below. \n\n![](images/88/88ffe30ae5401e00502b35d851b216768aad69bf94236561617adf23e1ce058f.png)\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x,y)=30-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $x$ increases on $[2,5],$ and\n\n- $f(x,y)=30-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ decreases as $y$ increases on $[0,2].$\n\n![](images/ce/ce0d90127e1f14654f4b32a933f1eb6e76e054c03f19ca40c3f04116aa3c2c93.png)\n\nAs a result, the *maximum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion. \n\n![](images/5b/5b9967c814e46914e0409854de0960e85339adc9b9fd9693677c8e048c342702.png)\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{ij} & =f({x}_{i-1},{y}_{j-1})=30-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor all $1\\le i\\le m$ and $1\\le j\\le n.$\n\nFinally, the upper Riemann sum is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}U(f,P) & ={\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}(30-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2})Δ{x}_{i}Δ{y}_{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing expression is $30-{x}_{i-1}^{2}-{y}_{j-1}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544877 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186179667 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "db8e7d68-5731-5a44-b86e-919a13689540" :knowledge-point/title "Writing an Upper Riemann Sum for a Strictly Increasing Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4d72316c-66bc-5aea-a9e7-6ae3924fdf1c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544253} {:answer/id #uuid "75554437-49f0-5320-a65f-0aedc0fd5993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j-1}+15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544346} {:answer/id #uuid "8a6b0192-6189-5193-8e9a-847ececf5748" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i-1}+4{y}_{j-1}+15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544385} {:answer/id #uuid "9cd98c1d-703c-597a-8457-56abacc2ec64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544426} {:answer/id #uuid "bcbfcef9-9540-5f6a-8359-e4e8e23a7772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j}+15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bcbfcef9-9540-5f6a-8359-e4e8e23a7772" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{i}+4{y}_{j}+15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544486} :answer-field/id #uuid "35349d98-38cf-51b3-a918-6967ce0df8e3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-fiel